---
/**
 * /teaching/fifteen-terms: the 15 essential Claude Code terms, as a rap, set as a lab sheet.
 *
 * Every row of the sheet sits in the page grid: the field name in the label column,
 * the work beside it. Step 1 is the lyric sheet that plays (components/rap/Player).
 * The checkpoint is a five-question quiz that reuses the Lab 01 checkbox
 * (components/rap/Quiz). After the sheet: every term printed for reading with the
 * sound off, the original video, and how it was made.
 *
 * Sources: /facts/rap-LYRICS.md (lyrics, verbatim), rap-timings.csv, rap-track_words.json,
 * rap-PROMPT_HISTORY.md, and the intensive's recordings index, which lists the rap and
 * the prompt walkthrough in Session 1 on Day 1.
 */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Sheet from '../../components/Sheet.astro';
import Overprint from '../../components/Overprint.astro';
import SectionHead from '../../components/SectionHead.astro';
import Player from '../../components/rap/Player.astro';
import Quiz from '../../components/rap/Quiz.astro';
import Glossary from '../../components/rap/Glossary.astro';
import RapVideo from '../../components/rap/RapVideo.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Fifteen Claude Code terms, in one song"
  description="A rap Andrew Yu made with Claude for Claude Dojo that teaches the 15 Claude Code terms a beginner meets first, with a lyric sheet that follows the song and a five-question check."
>
  <Sheet label="Lab 04 · Fifteen terms" meta="Time: 4 minutes" labelledby="rap-title" class="rap">
    <header class="top">
      <Overprint as="h1" id="rap-title" text="Fifteen Claude Code terms, in one song." />
      <div class="made spot">
        <p class="field">Made for Claude Dojo</p>
        <p>
          A rap I made with Claude. We played it for the room on Day 1 of the two-day intensive in July 2026.
        </p>
        <a class="more" href="/work/claude-dojo">Read the Claude Dojo case study</a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="g brief">
      <h2 class="field">Objective</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Learn the fifteen terms a beginner meets first in Claude Code, in the order you meet them. Play the song and follow
        the lyric sheet, or read every term below with the sound off.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="g step">
      <h2 class="field">Step 1 <span class="step__what">Listen</span></h2>
      <div>
        <Player />
        <p class="note">Pick a number to jump to that verse.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="g cp">
      <h2 class="field">Checkpoint <span class="step__what">Check yourself</span></h2>
      <div>
        <p class="cp__q">
          The song ends by testing you on one: a standard way to plug your tools into Claude. That is MCP. Now try five
          more. Tick the term for each definition.
        </p>
        <Quiz />
      </div>
    </div>
  </Sheet>

  <section class="sec" id="terms" aria-labelledby="terms-h">
    <SectionHead title="The fifteen terms" id="terms-h">
      Each one with what its verse says it means, and the verse itself, in the order the song teaches them.
    </SectionHead>
    <Glossary />
  </section>

  <section class="sec" id="video" aria-labelledby="video-h">
    <SectionHead title="The original video" id="video-h">
      Slides and word cards built in code and put together with ffmpeg. No filming, and no real people in it.
    </SectionHead>
    <div class="g g--plain">
      <span></span>
      <RapVideo>3 minutes 40 seconds, 720p, with the same track.</RapVideo>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-h">
    <SectionHead title="How it was made" id="how-h">A cheap version first, the polished one only after the words were locked.</SectionHead>
    <div class="g g--plain">
      <span></span>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          I made it with Claude. I supplied the term list from the course and the prompts, and Claude drafted the lyrics
          and revised them as I pushed. The shape came from a homemade hotkeys rap I had seen: a spoken intro, a numbered
          countdown, a breather in the middle, and a spoken outro.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before Claude made anything, I asked it to ask me questions. That turned a vague wish into four decisions
          about format, terms, audience, and how the music would get made. Then I asked
          for the terms in the order a learner meets them, and later for more rhymes.
        </p>
        <p>
          Then I built a cheap proof of concept. Claude Code turned the lyrics into slides, my cloned voice read them over a
          drum loop it wrote in Python, and ffmpeg put it together. A cloned voice cannot really rap, but it let me fix the
          words for almost nothing. Only once the content was locked did I spend on the polished version: I generated the
          track with Suno from the lyrics and a style prompt, and Claude Code retimed every slide to it from a word-level
          transcription of the song.
        </p>
        <p>
          I asked whether the video could recreate the faces of the real people in the
          video that inspired it. Claude said no. Those people are private individuals, several of them children, and they
          never agreed to it. I took the no, and the video uses original cards instead. I wrote down the lesson for the
          room:
        </p>
        <blockquote>
          <p>A good AI workflow includes hearing “no” sometimes.</p>
        </blockquote>
        <p>
          On Day 1 of the intensive we played the rap, and then I walked the room through the prompts that made it, one at
          a time. Here is that walkthrough, uncut.
        </p>
        <figure class="walkthrough" id="walkthrough">
          <video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="/media/rap-prompt-walkthrough-poster.jpg">
            <source src="/media/rap-prompt-walkthrough.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
            <track kind="captions" srclang="en" label="English" src="/media/rap-prompt-walkthrough.vtt" default />
          </video>
          <figcaption>
            I walk the room through the prompt history at the Claude Dojo intensive, Day 1, July 11, 2026. 2 minutes 54
            seconds, from the session recording, with captions. One name is muted and blurred because that person is not
            part of the course.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="credit label">
          Lyrics drafted by Claude from Andrew Yu's term list and prompts. Music generated with Suno from those lyrics. Video
          built with Claude Code.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .g {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: var(--cols);
    gap: var(--col-gap);
    padding: 24px 0;
    border-top: var(--rule-dash);
  }
  .g > .field {
    margin: 0;
    padding-top: 4px;
  }
  .g--plain {
    border-top: 0;
    padding-top: 30px;
  }

  .top {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 6.6fr) minmax(0, 3.4fr);
    gap: clamp(24px, 3.4vw, 52px);
    align-items: end;
    padding: clamp(26px, 4vw, 52px) 0 clamp(26px, 3.4vw, 40px);
  }
  .top :global(h1) {
    font-size: var(--step-hero);
    max-width: 16ch;
  }
  .made {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    justify-items: start;
    padding: clamp(20px, 2.2vw, 28px);
    font-size: var(--step-small);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .made .field {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .made .more {
    margin-top: 4px;
  }

  .brief {
    border-top: var(--rule);
  }
  .lede {
    max-width: 46ch;
  }

  .step__what {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 6px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-stretch: var(--w-title);
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    text-transform: none;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .step {
    padding-bottom: 34px;
  }
  .note {
    margin-top: 18px;
    font-size: var(--step-small);
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--text-soft);
  }

  .cp {
    border-top: var(--rule);
  }
  .cp__q {
    font-size: var(--step-body);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text-soft);
    max-width: 58ch;
    margin-bottom: 22px;
  }

  .credit {
    margin-top: 2em;
    padding-top: 14px;
    border-top: var(--rule);
  }

  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .top {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .g {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 14px;
    }
    .g--plain > span {
      display: none;
    }
    .step__what {
      display: inline;
      margin-left: 8px;
      font-size: 1.375rem;
    }
  }
  .walkthrough {
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }
  .walkthrough video {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--ink);
    background: var(--stock);
  }
</style>
